    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Adult granulosa cell tumor with thecoma-like foci.",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "This slide predominantly demonstrates a fibromatous background with less than 10% thecoma-like areas. Overall, it is challenging to identify classic adult granulosa cell tumor morphology on this slide without the aid of reticulin and examination of additional slides. The thecoma-like areas showed&nbsp;reticulin wrapping around clusters of cells, and further sampling of the tumor revealed greater than 10% of thecoma-like areas admixed with typical adult granulosa cell tumor morphology. The overall morphologic impression is further supported by reticulin staining pattern and FOXL2 mutation positivity, confirming the above diagnosis. Overall, the sex cord-stromal tumor with fibrothecomatous background warrant morphologic scrutiny to characterize typical adult granulosa cell tumor foci and at least a reticulin staining.",
    "source": "Zehra Ordulu",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
